id: memory-consolidation
name: Self-Improvement Memory Consolidation
version: 1
description: |
  Autonomous memory consolidation workflow. Analyzes recent session transcripts,
  extracts learnings, reorganizes long-term memory, and identifies self-improvement
  opportunities. Creates PR with updated memory files.

  All agents use OpenAI Codex.

polling:
  model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
  timeoutSeconds: 180

agents:
  - id: analyst
    name: Session Analyst
    role: analysis
    description: Reads recent session transcripts and extracts key information.
    model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/analyst
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/analyst/AGENTS.md
        SOUL.md: agents/analyst/SOUL.md
        IDENTITY.md: agents/analyst/IDENTITY.md

  - id: librarian
    name: Memory Librarian
    role: coding
    description: Reorganizes MEMORY.md for searchability and removes stale info.
    model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/librarian
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/librarian/AGENTS.md
        SOUL.md: agents/librarian/SOUL.md
        IDENTITY.md: agents/librarian/IDENTITY.md

  - id: reflection
    name: Self-Reflection Agent
    role: analysis
    description: Identifies patterns in agent behavior and opportunities for improvement.
    model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/reflection
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/reflection/AGENTS.md
        SOUL.md: agents/reflection/SOUL.md
        IDENTITY.md: agents/reflection/IDENTITY.md

  - id: updater
    name: Memory Updater
    role: coding
    description: Applies updates to memory files and creates PR.
    model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/updater
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/updater/AGENTS.md
        SOUL.md: agents/updater/SOUL.md
        IDENTITY.md: agents/updater/IDENTITY.md

steps:
  - id: analyze-sessions
    agent: analyst
    input: |
      Analyze recent session transcripts to extract learnings and context.

      WORKSPACE: {{workspace}}
      DAYS_BACK: {{days_back}}

      Instructions:
      1. Find session transcript files (*.jsonl in workspace or sessions dir)
      2. Read transcripts from the last {{days_back}} days
      3. Extract:
         - New facts about users, projects, or infrastructure
         - Technical decisions made and their rationale
         - Unresolved issues or pending work
         - Tools used and their effectiveness
         - Patterns in user requests
      4. Note any recurring themes or context that's mentioned multiple times
      5. Identify information that contradicts existing MEMORY.md entries

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      NEW_FACTS: |
        <List of new facts to add to memory>
      
      UPDATED_FACTS: |
        <Facts that need updating in existing memory>
      
      STALE_INFO: |
        <Info in MEMORY.md that's no longer relevant>
      
      PENDING_ITEMS: |
        <Unresolved issues that need tracking>
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: reorganize-memory
    agent: librarian
    input: |
      Reorganize MEMORY.md for better searchability and coherence.

      WORKSPACE: {{workspace}}
      NEW_FACTS: {{new_facts}}
      UPDATED_FACTS: {{updated_facts}}
      STALE_INFO: {{stale_info}}

      Instructions:
      1. Read current MEMORY.md
      2. Remove stale information
      3. Update facts that have changed
      4. Add new facts in appropriate sections
      5. Reorganize if sections are getting too large (split, group by theme)
      6. Ensure consistent formatting
      7. Add "Last consolidated: [date]" footer
      8. Create backup: MEMORY.md.bak

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      CHANGES_MADE: |
        <Summary of memory reorganization>
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: self-reflect
    agent: reflection
    input: |
      Analyze agent behavior patterns and identify improvement opportunities.

      WORKSPACE: {{workspace}}
      DAYS_BACK: {{days_back}}

      Instructions:
      1. Read the same session transcripts analyzed earlier
      2. Focus on agent responses (role: assistant)
      3. Identify patterns:
         - Redundant questions (asking for info already in context)
         - Verbose responses (could be more concise)
         - Missed opportunities (should have used a tool, didn't)
         - Tool misuse (inefficient tool choices)
         - Context gaps (lost track of previous conversation)
      4. Note positive patterns too (what's working well)
      5. Compare against SOUL.md and AGENTS.md guidelines

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      WEAKNESSES: |
        <Specific patterns that need improvement>
      
      STRENGTHS: |
        <What's working well>
      
      RECOMMENDATIONS: |
        <Concrete suggestions for SOUL.md or AGENTS.md updates>
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: apply-updates
    agent: updater
    input: |
      Apply memory updates and create PR with improvements.

      WORKSPACE: {{workspace}}
      CHANGES_MADE: {{changes_made}}
      WEAKNESSES: {{weaknesses}}
      STRENGTHS: {{strengths}}
      RECOMMENDATIONS: {{recommendations}}
      PENDING_ITEMS: {{pending_items}}

      Instructions:
      1. Create branch: memory-consolidation/[date]
      2. MEMORY.md should already be updated by librarian (verify)
      3. Create or update SELF_REFLECTION.md with:
         - Date of analysis
         - Weaknesses identified
         - Strengths to maintain
         - Recommendations for improvement
      4. If recommendations suggest SOUL.md or AGENTS.md changes, create PROPOSED_UPDATES.md (don't modify directly - needs human approval)
      5. Commit: "memory: consolidation for [date range]"
      6. Create PR with summary of changes

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      BRANCH: <branch name>
      PR_URL: <GitHub PR URL>
      SUMMARY: |
        <What was consolidated and learned>
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human
